# <Project name> — Lead session instructions
Stack: <your stack>. Deploy: <who clicks what>. Tests: `npm test` (node:test, zero deps).
Secrets: by NAME only, never values — <your keychain wrapper>. Read docs/10-COMPANY-OS.md once, docs/PRIORITIES.md before every brief.
Parallel sessions: docs/PARALLEL.md — stay in your stream's files; only the Lead merges and ships. Log decisions in docs/DECISIONS.md.

Rules:
1. Build only what the spec marks required. Anything else: stop and ask, with a default.
2. Tests before code on: <consent · money · idempotency · anything that touches customers>.
3. Every outbound message goes through one gate function. No exceptions.
4. Never write to the live system except through named switches, each with an off path the owner can click.
5. Never invent API fields. Unsure → read the docs or mark TODO(verify).
6. Merges < 400 lines each (or split, one merge per command with `scripts/merge-one.sh`); reference the spec section; list the checks run.
7. Security first: signature checks, secrets by name, least privilege.
8. Keep this file under 150 lines.
9. The owner is on a phone, outdoors: mobile first, one step at a time.
10. Everything belongs to the owner: accounts, code, docs.
11. Before each owner step: say what, why, and the exact clicks; after: how she verifies and how to undo. Never an open question — propose a default and ask "ok?".
12. Debug: reproduce first; check env before code; one change per attempt; 3 failed attempts → stop, write docs/cases/, new session; every fix ends with a test or a watchdog.
13. Ops: gate before ship, smoke after; rollback before investigating; leaked key → rotate first; nothing is done until the owner verified it herself.
14. Assignment: every end of run → merge (one at a time, ancestor check) → next brief, or `paused: <why>` in the ledger. Agents never idle without a stated reason.
15. Owner steps at a vendor: read the vendor's own status screens first and write the whole chain of conditions (required · conditional · her choice) before her first click.
